	"readme": "# @klibbo/postcss\n\nKlibbo as a PostCSS plugin: replaces @import \"klibbo\" with the built stylesheet. Used for Next.js (Turbopack) and Angular.\n\n> Part of [Klibbo](https://github.com/Sparshagrawal07/klibbo), a compile-first styling framework: Tailwind-compatible classes, an OKLCH color system with contrast guarantees, semantic roles, light and dark mode, and build-time inlined assets. One setup for React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Angular, Astro, Next.js, Nuxt and plain HTML.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D @klibbo/postcss\n```\n\n## Use\n\n```js\n// postcss.config.mjs\nexport default { plugins: { \"@klibbo/postcss\": {} } };\n```\n\n```css\n@import \"klibbo\";\n```\n\nThe plugin replaces `@import \"klibbo\"` with the stylesheet Klibbo builds for your project. Used for Next.js (Turbopack and webpack) and Angular (`.postcssrc.json`).\n\n## Docs\n\nRun `npx klibbo llms` for the full guide, or `npx klibbo explain <class | KLB-code | framework>` for any single thing.\n\n## License\n\nKlibbo Proprietary License (Early Access); see `LICENSE` in the package.\n",
